  <content>{{velocity}}
## Inputs, set by the sheet of the entry, which includes this page in edit mode:
## - $entryObject
## - $changeObject
## A migration note is what to do when upgrading, which its title and its description say: those are the only fields
## an author fills. The audience, the category, the importance and the media of a change mean nothing for a note,
## and keep the values the change template gives them, the importance included, which the notes are ordered on.
## The product, the version and the type of the entry are given by the release note the note was added from, and
## the form carries them along so that saving the form stores them.
(% class='xform col-xs-12' %)(((
#displayEntryField($changeObject, 'title', '')
#displayEntryField($changeObject, 'description', '')
$doc.display('product', 'hidden', $entryObject)
$doc.display('version', 'hidden', $entryObject)
$doc.display('type', 'hidden', $entryObject)
)))
{{/velocity}}</content>
